{{! mcp.json.tmpl: the per-run MCP registration, <run>/mcp.json, passed to Claude Code as
  --strict-mcp-config --mcp-config <run>/mcp.json; runtimes with other registration formats get the same
  server through their own per-run config. keel api mcp serves two read tools (keel_context, keel_arch)
  and one outbox-only write tool (keel_submit), each validated by the Steward at ingest.
  Rendering: scalar values are escaped for a JSON string; tokens ending in _json are inserted as JSON.
  keel_command_json is keel's resolved executable; keel_args_json holds its script path (if any) followed
  by api and mcp. mcp_env_json carries only keel's own run variables (KEEL_RUN_ID), never a provider
  value; it is an empty object when the snippet is printed for interactive use.
  Whether MCP servers run outside a runtime's tool sandbox: verification_status unverified. }}
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "keel": {
      "command": {{keel_command_json}},
      "args": {{keel_args_json}},
      "env": {{mcp_env_json}}
    }
  }
}
